In a discussion initiated by a user, key points from a reading on the economic risks of climate change, authored by Delavane Diaz and Frances Moore, were summarized. The article emphasizes the challenge of quantifying the social cost of carbon (SCC) due to complex interactions in Earth and human systems. It highlights the limitations of damage functions used in integrated assessment models (IAMs) like DICE, FUND, and PAGE, which aim to translate climate variables into economic losses but often fail to capture recent scientific advancements. In response, a set of multiple-choice questions was proposed to assess students' understanding of the reading, focusing on concepts like SCC, damage functions, and dynamic vulnerability within IAMs.
